  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d4f101f-51a0-4563-a24d-896d6c056953",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11.8 Converting Date Columns into Datetime Format\n",
    "\n",
    "Date columns are initially stored as object data types. Converting them into datetime format allows us to perform date-based analysis, calculate time differences, and identify trends over time."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "fd86f464-afca-493b-80ae-4370b9ab0f11",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Convert date columns into datetime format\n",
    "\n",
    "date_columns = [\n",
    "    'manufacture_date',\n",
    "    'observation_date',\n",
    "    'last_service_date'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "for col in date_columns:\n",
    "    df[col] = pd.to_datetime(df[col], errors='coerce')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "990f27fb-e552-4d39-b5f3-0181abbc97cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "manufacture_date     datetime64[us]\n",
       "observation_date     datetime64[us]\n",
       "last_service_date    datetime64[us]\n",
       "dtype: object"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 28,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Verify converted date column data types\n",
    "\n",
    "df[date_columns].dtypes"
   ]
  },
