  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0096eed7-2922-46c4-8780-236764c22a04",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11.52 Handling Missing Numerical Values Using Median\n",
    "\n",
    "In this step, we replace missing values in numerical columns with their respective median values to reduce missing data while minimizing the influence of outliers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 111,
   "id": "98bdd16d-7c06-4dff-a8ba-b766063614f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Missing values in numerical columns after median imputation:\n",
      "Series([], dtype: int64)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Select numerical columns\n",
    "\n",
    "numerical_columns = df.select_dtypes(\n",
    "    include='number'\n",
    ").columns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fill missing values using median\n",
    "\n",
    "for column in numerical_columns:\n",
    "    df[column] = df[column].fillna(df[column].median())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Missing values in numerical columns after median imputation:\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    df[numerical_columns].isnull().sum()[\n",
    "        df[numerical_columns].isnull().sum() > 0\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "df33440f-1b8c-4bdc-a241-557ecef5e5b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 11.53 Handling Missing Values in Categorical Columns\n",
    "\n",
    "In this step, missing values in categorical columns are handled using the mode (most frequently occurring value)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 112,
   "id": "f1e06c3a-2c03-494c-812c-5100f140c44a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Missing values in categorical columns after imputation:\n",
      "battery_id              0\n",
      "observation_id          0\n",
      "chemistry               0\n",
      "manufacturer            0\n",
      "vehicle_model           0\n",
      "climate_zone            0\n",
      "bms_firmware_version    0\n",
      "failure_risk_label      0\n",
      "degradation_category    0\n",
      "dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "C:\\Users\\ajmal\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\ipykernel_21340\\1436226636.py:2: Pandas4Warning: For backward compatibility, 'str' dtypes are included by select_dtypes when 'object' dtype is specified. This behavior is deprecated and will be removed in a future version. Explicitly pass 'str' to `include` to select them, or to `exclude` to remove them and silence this warning.\n",
      "See https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/migration-3-strings.html#string-migration-select-dtypes for details on how to write code that works with pandas 2 and 3.\n",
      "  categorical_columns = df.select_dtypes(include='object').columns\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Select categorical columns\n",
    "categorical_columns = df.select_dtypes(include='object').columns\n",
    "\n",
    "# Fill missing values using mode\n",
    "for column in categorical_columns:\n",
    "    if df[column].isnull().sum() > 0:\n",
    "        df[column] = df[column].fillna(df[column].mode()[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check missing values\n",
